WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.913
Aktion T4.

00:00:01.863 --> 00:00:03.647
Nazi Germany.

00:00:03.647 --> 00:00:06.909
1939 to 1945.

00:00:06.909 --> 00:00:08.829
Framed as mercy.

00:00:08.829 --> 00:00:11.170
Started with terminal illness.

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:13.318
Expanded to disability.

00:00:13.318 --> 00:00:16.125
Then eliminated the program's critics.

00:00:16.125 --> 00:00:18.352
The pattern is documented.

00:00:18.352 --> 00:00:20.397
The pattern is repeating.

00:00:20.397 --> 00:00:21.727
Canada.

00:00:21.727 --> 00:00:22.999
MAID.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.499
2016 to present.

00:00:25.499 --> 00:00:27.477
Framed as compassion.

00:00:27.477 --> 00:00:29.818
Started with terminal illness.

00:00:29.818 --> 00:00:32.454
Expanded to non-terminal conditions.

00:00:32.454 --> 00:00:35.624
Mental illness approved for 2027.

00:00:35.624 --> 00:00:40.647
Both programs preceded by propaganda framing vulnerable populations as burdens.

00:00:40.647 --> 00:00:46.284
Both featured government cost-benefit analyses supporting the elimination of specific demographics.

00:00:46.284 --> 00:00:50.704
MAID deaths: one thousand and eighteen in 2016.

00:00:50.704 --> 00:00:55.056
Sixteen thousand, two hundred and sixty-seven in 2024.

00:00:55.056 --> 00:00:57.545
Fifteen hundred percent growth.

00:00:57.545 --> 00:01:00.113
The comparison is not rhetorical.

00:01:00.113 --> 00:01:02.579
The trajectory is mathematical.

00:01:02.579 --> 00:01:05.352
The government's own numbers make the case.
